{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumWuYNBACtGDr191u4m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the `--repeats` flag, for example `npx vitest run --repeats 10`. It reruns every test the number of times you give it, whether the test passes or fails, so a flaky test will show up as an intermittent failure. I confirmed the flag in this project's installed Vitest CLI, where it's described as \"Repeat every test a specific number of times regardless of the result (default: `0`)\". Since the default is 0, the number probably counts extra runs after the first, so `--repeats 10` would run each test 11 times. Don't confuse it with `--retry`: that only reruns tests that failed, which hides flakiness instead of exposing it. To focus on one suspect test, add `-t \"<pattern>\"`. In Vitest 5 the pattern is matched against the full name, meaning the suite names plus the test name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":23575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a0d0ae2-225f-4c0a-bbfa-d8f32cbd97db","uuid":"4f9dd250-0c70-452b-bd70-3543361e9e62","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:50:10.017Z","request_id":"req_011CfumWuJESXPSqR2ijTqtY"}
